    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Given a dataset of credit card transactions with features such as transaction amount, merchant category, device trust score, and location mismatch, the objective is to build a machine learning model that predicts whether a transaction is fraudulent (is_fraud = 1) or not (is_fraud = 0). The challenge lies in handling class imbalance, ensuring no data leakage, and optimizing evaluation metrics beyond accuracy (precision, recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC) to minimize both false positives and false negatives. The solution will help financial institutions reduce monetary losses and improve customer trust."
      ],
